	That's not really all that bad. Knights are Wis-based casters,
so the low Int only hurts your chances of learning spells (and Wis can
be exercised, so even if that's low too, it won't be by the time you
need it). By the time you get the Mirror, you should have no trouble
blessing spellbooks (or just getting them pre-blessed from Lugh), which
eliminates even that problem.

	And the high Strength is a sizable advantage in the early game,
not least because it means you can carry around all that armor they
loaded you with, and that massively heavy lance.

